# Hand-built IE block (RFC 5456 §8.6) for a realistic NEW full-frame payload.
# This is the payload block only (12-byte full-frame header is IAX-1's
# concern, not this parser's) -- five IEs back to back, VERSION first as
# §8.6.10 requires on NEW ("MUST include the 'version' IE, and it MUST be
# the first IE; the order of other IEs is unspecified").
#
# Field-by-field:
#   0b 02 0002              -- §8.6.10 VERSION (0x0b): len 2, value 0x0002
#   01 05 3535353533        -- §8.6.1 CALLED_NUMBER (0x01): len 5, ASCII "55553"
#   06 06 4b4331414243      -- §8.6.6 USERNAME (0x06): len 6, ASCII "KC1ABC"
#   08 04 00000006          -- §8.6.7/§8.7 CAPABILITY (0x08): len 4, bitmask
#                               0x00000006 = GSM Full Rate (1<<1) | G.711 mu-law (1<<2)
#   09 04 00000004          -- §8.6.8/§8.7 FORMAT (0x09): len 4, single bit
#                               0x00000004 = G.711 mu-law (notes §8)
0b 02 00 02  01 05 35 35 35 35 33  06 06 4b 43 31 41 42 43  08 04 00 00 00 06  09 04 00 00 00 04
